    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "The issue is that the new rule-based system won't have your capacity for pattern recognition. It's strictly going to follow the hard-coded parameters. If something happens that isn't explicitly covered in the new code—like a novel sensor failure pattern or a 'black swan' mechanical event—the new system just won't flag it. It'll only see what it's programmed to see.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That's a fair point. To mitigate this, I'll work with the compliance team to incorporate comprehensive scenarios into the rule-based system from the start, including 'black swan' events. For any anomalies that were previously patterns but are now outliers, I'll propose a manual review process. We can create a temporary task force to analyze and write new rules for these unexpected events so they can be included in the next update cycle. Additionally, I'll enhance logging to ensure that these occurrences are flagged for immediate investigation. Our goal is to get as close as possible to the foresight provided by neural-probabilistic modeling within the confines of the new deterministic system.",
      "source": "target",
